      "procedure": "Procedure\nPreheat oven to 175°C.\nIn a large bowl, combine flour, sugar, cocoa powder, baking soda and salt. Set aside.\nIn another bowl, whisk together eggs, butter, vanilla extract and warm water until well combined. Add in dry mixture and, mix until smooth.\nLine an 8 inch baking pan with parchment paper and pour in cake batter. Bake for 24-26 minutes. Once cooked, chill for 15-20 minutes.\nUnmold cooled chocolate cake into a large bowl, then break apart and mash. Add chocolate frosting, and mix until it forms a dough. Use an ice cream scooper to form into balls. Refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.\nInsert Pocky stick into the center of each chilled cake balls. Freeze for another 10 minutes or until firm.\nMelt dark chocolate in a double boiler. Dip cake ball in melted chocolate until fully coated. Then coat with desired sprinkles. Place back on baking sheet and freeze for an hour of until it sets."
