      "procedure": "Procedure\nCombine chocolate cookies and butter. Fill the bottom of an 8-inch springform pan with the cookie mixture, and press it in to form a crust. Chill for 30 minutes.\nUsing a double boiler, melt dark chocolate until smooth.\nIn a small bowl, whisk together gelatin and water, then let bloom. \nPour ½ cup heavy cream in a small pot, then bring to a bare simmer. Mix in bloomed gelatin, and whisk until fully dissolved. Mix in melted chocolate.\nWhip remaining heavy cream and confectioners sugar until stiff peaks form.\nGently fold in chocolate mixture into the whipped cream. \nSlice 4 pcs. of Ferrero Chocolate in half, then stick onto the sides of an 8 inch springform pan. Carefully fill the pan with the chocolate mousse, then smoothen the top. Chill for 3 hours, \nTop with more Ferrero Chocolate, royal icing roses and sugar crystals."
